    "description": "## Objective\n\nEnable Person Accounts in the build sandbox so Players and Referrers can be modeled as B2C-style people with account-level relationships.\n\n## Implementation Requirements\n\n* Verify org prerequisites: a default Account record type exists, and Account/Contact organization-wide defaults are set to Controlled by Parent (or aligned)\n* Enable Person Accounts (raise the Salesforce support case if the setup toggle is unavailable in this org)\n* Create one test Person Account to confirm enablement, then delete it\n* Document what configuration carried into this partial sandbox from production (record types, apps, installed packages)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n* Person Accounts are enabled\n* A test Person Account can be created and deleted\n* Prerequisite settings documented\n\n## Testing Notes\n\nCreate/delete one test Person Account.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\nPlayer/Referrer record types and fields (POC-08). Permission model (BUILD-01).\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n* Person Account enablement is irreversible.\n* Production requires its own enablement before deployment and may need a Salesforce support case — start the production request in parallel so the sandbox-to-prod deployment is not blocked later.\n\n---\n\nEstimate: S · \\~4h · Dependencies: None — do first · Ticket POC-01 (approved 2026-07-04)",
